WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.417
This is DRAFT, your strategic assistant for League of Legends.

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:10.572
This video presents the app and shows step by step how to use it.

00:00:11.872 --> 00:00:17.964
During champion select, DRAFT helps you choose, among the champions you play,

00:00:17.964 --> 00:00:21.525
the one that best fits the enemy composition.

00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:25.244
It explains its choice with a simple game plan.

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:31.336
Your data stays on your PC, and it never acts in the client: you always pick,

00:00:31.336 --> 00:00:33.314
ban and lock in yourself.

00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:36.698
Step one: launch DRAFT.

00:00:36.698 --> 00:00:41.319
No window opens; an icon appears next to the clock.

00:00:41.319 --> 00:00:49.111
Right-clicking this icon gives access to the main window, the panels and the settings.

00:00:49.111 --> 00:00:52.916
No key and no account are needed to start.

00:00:54.216 --> 00:00:56.673
Step two: open the settings.

00:00:56.673 --> 00:01:02.902
In My profiles, choose a role, then add your champions with the search.

00:01:02.902 --> 00:01:07.289
Each role keeps its own pool, saved automatically.

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:12.992
You can also export your profiles to a file and import them back.

00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:16.778
Step three: choose your role.

00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:22.522
The five icons at the top of each window switch roles in one click.

00:01:22.522 --> 00:01:25.780
The active role is shown next to them.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.902
Step four: enter the enemy champions as they are picked.

00:01:31.902 --> 00:01:34.486
Type a name, then press Enter.

00:01:34.486 --> 00:01:40.686
DRAFT guesses each opponent's role, and you can correct it in one click.

00:01:40.686 --> 00:01:44.647
The recommendation updates with each addition.

00:01:45.947 --> 00:01:48.574
Step five: read the recommendation.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:52.551
In the center, the suggested champion from your pool,

00:01:52.551 --> 00:01:56.303
with an alternative and the reason for the choice.

00:01:56.303 --> 00:02:00.281
At the bottom, every champion in your pool is ranked.

00:02:00.281 --> 00:02:05.834
On the right, the game plan: how to win, threats, targets and useful bans.

00:02:07.134 --> 00:02:12.945
During champion select, you can use compact panels placed next to the client.

00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:19.436
They show the essentials: the recommendation, the enemy composition and the game plan.

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:23.744
To go further, several tabs are available.

00:02:23.744 --> 00:02:31.478
Analysis details the criteria behind the choice and compares two of your champions against this composition.

00:02:31.478 --> 00:02:34.056
Tips gives educational explanations.

00:02:34.056 --> 00:02:39.928
Duel shows what to pick against a specific mid laner, without touching your draft.

00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:47.619
DRAFT uses the Riot Games API for optional features, always started by you.

00:02:47.619 --> 00:02:51.964
The first one: importing your ranked match history.

00:02:51.964 --> 00:02:58.525
You enter your Riot ID, your region and how many games to read, then confirm.

00:02:59.825 --> 00:03:04.365
Concretely, DRAFT calls account-v1 to find your account,

00:03:04.365 --> 00:03:10.202
then match-v5 to list your ranked solo/duo games and read their details.

00:03:10.202 --> 00:03:17.823
For each game, DRAFT keeps on your PC the date, patch, duration, your champion, your position,

00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:21.634
the result, your K/D/A and the enemy champions.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.742
No other player is stored.

00:03:23.742 --> 00:03:29.985
The key is sent in the request header, never in the URL, and it is not saved.

00:03:29.985 --> 00:03:37.038
Rate limits are respected: if the API answers 429, DRAFT waits for the indicated delay.

00:03:38.338 --> 00:03:45.490
Once your history is imported, the Games tab summarizes your most played champions and your results.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:52.283
DRAFT also points out your most familiar champion, without ever changing the strategic ranking.

00:03:52.283 --> 00:03:54.715
The data shown here is fictitious.

00:03:56.015 --> 00:03:58.501
DRAFT follows strict rules.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:02.645
It automates nothing: no picking, no banning.

00:04:02.645 --> 00:04:08.539
It only uses information already visible during champion select,

00:04:08.539 --> 00:04:11.946
plus general per-champion statistics.

00:04:11.946 --> 00:04:14.525
No data is sent to a server.

00:04:14.525 --> 00:04:18.761
Client reading is optional and off by default.

00:04:20.061 --> 00:04:24.185
Thank you for watching this presentation of DRAFT.
